Z||000033||Rob||12-03-1999||03:53 PM||||  I drive my car about 4000 miles to and from work everyday of the summer. <BR>  The six months of snow we have just kinda bites so it has to rest all winter. ||||reg||1
Z||000034||Phaeton||12-04-1999||05:26 PM||||Here in Fairbanks it is winter from september to may.  With four skinny studded tires the Fiero is one of the best handling snow cars available.  The balance and traction are such that all wheel drive vehicles just don't keep up except in very deep new snow.  With only four hours of daylight right now the daily rush of driving keeps my inner world bright and cheerful.  Luckily the snow berms are high enough to catch the car gently when I slide off the road, so far no body panels have cracked and all the experience with four wheel drifts does translate over to high speed pavement driving.  Out of twenty five Fiero's in the area I only see two others on the road during the winter, those guys that park theirs are missing the whole point of owning a fine driving car.||||reg||1
Z||000035||Jim Baumann||12-05-1999||06:03 PM||||As soon as I get my new engine in I will be driving my 86 GT 40 miles every day.<p>[This message has been edited by Jim Baumann (edited 12-05-1999).]||||reg||6
Z||000036||fierosound||12-05-1999||11:09 PM||||1987 GT (bought in 1990 - I'm second owner)  Driven year round winter/summer (Calgary, Canada).  We do get some snow, but not all that much - but head out to the mountains!!!<P>I came back from a mountain crossing with terrrible salt/sand/slush road conditions.  People were staring at my poor car - a mudball on wheels, the only clean spots were the windshield "wiper tracks" and rear window!!<P>A quick stop at a car wash and a thorough wash remedied the problem.  Now at 155,000km, and still going strong.  Website at:  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierosound" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierosound</A> <P>||||reg||10
Z||000037||jlhuber||12-06-1999||12:52 AM||||i used to drive my 86.5 gt every day until i enlisted into the USAF.  now i drive an '89 ford ranger, but i miss my baby soo much, (she lives at parents house in michigan) so i am bringing her back out here (McGuire AFB New Jersey) when i go home for christmas vacation.  my daily milage to and from work is maybe two miles if i am lucky.  when i did have my fiero out here apirl 99- june 99, the drive to and from work was not long enough, so i'd get an itch to take her out 'crusin' on a nice day without the t-tops.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000038||Racer 1||12-06-1999||03:30 AM||||I drive my 86 coupe about 15 miles a week! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=159982&a=1168563&p=14192356&Sequence=2">  <A HREF="http://fierorob.homepage.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://fierorob.homepage.com/</A> <P>||||reg||6
Z||000039||stsmithgt||12-06-1999||12:25 PM||||Everyday 86 gt.  As long as it's not in the shop with some incompitant mechanic.  I just got back from dropping my car off again and they tried charging me AGAIN for the same problem.&gt; <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I'm about ready for the B.A.R. on these guys unfortunatly.  Three times is not a charm in this case.  Sorry about the Wah Wah attitude, but I need an informed, qualified mechanic.||||reg||8
Z||000040||PAUL88GT||12-06-1999||01:06 PM||||I drive my 88gt to work (20 mile rd trip)and on weekends when it is not raining.  It stays in my garage.  In fact, the sunroof glass is removed most of the time. ||||reg||7
Z||000041||BlackGT||12-07-1999||01:46 AM||||My 86GT is my only car and besides I wouldn`t want to drive anything else! One other thing since my employer pays for my mileage not only is it fun to drive but I get PAID TO DO IT!!!||||reg||1
Z||000042||Carrolles||12-07-1999||07:58 AM||||When I'm not on an out of town assignment I drive mine daily about 75 miles.  While I was flying back and forth between St. Louis and Birmingham every week my car spent most of its time at the airport.  Now that I am driving between Birmingham and Augusta, GA every week mine is in the engine replacement mode.<P>I've got the engine back in and am putting back all the junk.  I did install an Addco rear sway bar and am very pleased with it.  The new motor feels very good and the clutch is great.<P>I still have to install the power windows/locks and cruise control.<P>It is  silver 85SE v-6 4spd with tilt, rear defogger, am/fm tape, electric engine hatch release, power mirrors, luggage rack, sunroof.||||reg||1
Z||000043||hefty||12-07-1999||10:19 PM||||Every day. I just got back from a week long biz trip, think I'd go into withdraw if I had to stay away from it any longer than that ! Any body go to the NACE show in Atlanta ?||||reg||10
Z||000044||js||12-08-1999||02:24 AM||||I drive my Fiero every day to work about 27 miles roundtrip, and about 12k per year. 80% of it is interstate miles. This also includes driving in snow.||||reg||1
